# Pin YOUR scratch environments to a specific Fly region.
#
# You usually do NOT need this. With no pin anywhere, `make fly-up` asks Fly
# where to run and takes its answer - the anycast edge nearest you, the same
# thing `fly launch` would pick. Contributors are in different places, so that
# is the right default; this file is for when you want to override it.
#
# Copy to `.fly-region` - that name is gitignored, this one is not.
# `flyctl platform regions` lists them all. Common:
#   arn  Stockholm      fra  Frankfurt     lhr  London
#   iad  Virginia       sjc  San Jose      ord  Chicago
#   nrt  Tokyo          syd  Sydney        gru  Sao Paulo
#
# Overridden, most specific first, by:
#   make fly-up ENV=x REGION=fra     just this run
#   environments/<x>.yaml `region:`  a shared, named environment pins its own,
#                                    so it does not drift with whoever deploys
#   $FLY_REGION                      an ad-hoc shell default
#
# Only affects where NEW machines are placed - it does not move an environment
# that already exists.
fra
